      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.048,
            0.428,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.089,
            0.606,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "5. The pie chart on the right shows the result of a survey carried out to find the modes of transport used by children to go to school. Study the pie chart and answer the following questions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.192,
            0.607,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": "(i) What is the most common mode of transport?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.624,
            0.085,
            0.845,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.234,
            0.606,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "(ii) What fraction of children travel by car?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.276,
            0.847,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": "(iii) If 18 children travel by car, how many children took part in the survey? How many children use taxis to travel to school?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.319,
            0.848,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": "children travelling?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.362,
            0.847,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "6. Three workers can paint a fence in 4 days. If one more worker joins the team, how many days will it take them to finish the work? What are the assumptions you need to make?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.428,
            0.846,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "7. It takes 6 hours to fill 2 tanks of the same size with a pump. How long will it take to fill 5 such tanks with the same pump?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.476,
            0.847,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": "8. A given set of chairs are arranged in 25 rows, with 12 chairs in each row. If the chairs are rearranged with 20 chairs in each row, how many rows does this new arrangement have?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.542,
            0.847,
            0.6
          ],
          "content": "9. A school has 8 periods a day, each of 45 minutes duration. How long is each period, if the school has 9 periods a day, assuming that the number of school hours per day stays the same?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.608,
            0.624,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "10. A small pump can fill a tank in 3 hours, while a large pump can fill the same tank in 2 hours. If both pumps are used together, how long will the tank take to fill?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.65,
            0.607,
            0.819,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.693,
            0.521,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "11. A factory requires 42 machines to produce a given number of toys in 63 days. How many machines are required to produce the same number of toys in 54 days?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.796,
            0.522,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": "12. A car takes 2 hours to reach a destination, travelling at a speed of 60 km/h. How long will the car take if it travels at a speed of 80 km/h?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.699,
            0.911,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": "",
